msgid "Modem Watchdog"
msgstr ""

msgid "Detects stalled LTE bearers and recovers the interface automatically. Changes take effect after saving and restarting the daemon."
msgstr ""

msgid "Running"
msgstr ""

msgid "Stopped / not installed"
msgstr ""

msgid "Current Status"
msgstr ""

msgid "Service"
msgstr ""

msgid "Daemon status"
msgstr ""

msgid "Watchdog Behaviour"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enable watchdog"
msgstr ""

msgid "Turn the stall-detection watchdog on or off entirely."
msgstr ""

msgid "Auto mobile (detect movement)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Automatically switch to the 30s/5s handover-safe profile when the serving cell changes (the device is moving), and revert to the stationary profile after a period of stillness. Boots into the stationary profile, so a parked device is unaffected. ON by default."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mobile mode (force, manual)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Force the 30s/5s stall-detection profile at all times (car, travel router) instead of auto-detecting movement. Only shown when Auto mobile is OFF; with Auto mobile ON this is unnecessary."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mobile grace (seconds)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Keep the mobile profile this long after the last detected cell change before reverting to stationary."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cell poll (seconds)"
msgstr ""

msgid "How often the watchdog samples the serving cell over ModemManager D-Bus to detect movement. Read-only; never wedges the modem."
msgstr ""

msgid "Stall timeout (seconds)"
msgstr ""

msgid "How long the bearer is quiet before the watchdog declares a stall. Range 30–600; the manual_override config can set values below 30 but the script will clamp to 30."
msgstr ""

msgid "Check interval (seconds)"
msgstr ""

msgid "How often the watchdog checks RX counters."
msgstr ""

msgid "Recovery cooldown (seconds)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Minimum gap between consecutive recovery attempts, so a flaky tower cannot flap the interface back-to-back."
msgstr ""

msgid "Keepalive (normally off)"
msgstr ""

msgid "DNS keepalive"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sends a tiny DNS query every few minutes while idle to keep the modem’s RRC layer in RRC_CONNECTED. Stock Android does NOT do this — leave disabled unless you have a specific network that drops silent bearers."
msgstr ""

msgid "Keepalive interval (seconds)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Keepalive target"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hostname that get a DNS lookup each interval."
msgstr ""

msgid "Recovery escalation"
msgstr ""

msgid "Allow SSR restart (modem subsystem reset)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Stage-3 ladder: restart the modem remoteproc. Android’s stock bam_dmux calls subsystem_restart(\"modem\") on the same A2 timeout sites, so this is parity. Disable ONLY if you want the modem state frozen for post-mortem analysis."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bearer-down redrive (seconds)"
msgstr ""

msgid "A netifd \"down\" interface still down this long after a rebuild is stuck — the watchdog retriggers `ifup` and re-arms the proto."
msgstr ""

msgid "Zombie-modem nudge (seconds)"
msgstr ""

msgid "After a modem crash the baseband can land in a low-power zombie state (no modem object, no registration). This many seconds without a modem object triggers one qmicli --dms-set-operating-mode=online poke. Set to 0 to disable."
msgstr ""

msgid "Voice liveness hold"
msgstr ""

msgid "When the data bearer has no downlink, skip the recovery ladder (no interface rebuild, no SSR) while a call is in progress, or, for a SIM without data service, while the modem is alive for voice (IMS registered, or registered with live serving-cell measurements). Restarting the modem cannot bring data to a voice-only SIM."
msgstr ""

msgid "SIM data service"
msgstr ""

msgid "Auto (no downlink with this SIM since boot = no data service)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Data SIM (only a call holds the ladder)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Voice-only SIM"
msgstr ""

msgid "Auto tracks the SIM by ICCID: a SIM swap starts over, a modem restart does not. Any downlink packet ends the hold."
msgstr ""

msgid "Voice hold recheck (seconds)"
msgstr ""

msgid "How long a voice hold lasts before the watchdog checks again whether the modem is still alive for voice."
msgstr ""

msgid "Drop modem default route during hold"
msgstr ""

msgid "While a SIM without data service is held, remove the modem's default routes so traffic never falls back to the empty bearer (e.g. while the Wi-Fi station reconnects). Only while another uplink has a default route or had one in the last 5 minutes; with the modem as the only uplink the routes stay. They are restored when the hold ends. A data SIM keeps its routes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Watchdog restart requested; check status if anything looks wrong."
msgstr ""

